Package: AMDconfigurations
Type: Package
Title: Geometric Analysis of Configurations in High-Dimensional Spaces
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Manuel", "Mendoza", role = c("aut", "cre"),
  email = "mmendoza@mncn.csic.es",
  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2143-8138"))
Description: Computes Average Membership Degree (AMD) from soft-membership
    matrices and constructs AMD curves across candidate configuration counts.
    The current curve backend uses repeated fuzzy c-means fits while keeping
    the AMD definition, membership estimation, curve construction, and final
    assignment as separate operations. Fitted memberships, convergence
    diagnostics, preprocessing transformations, seeds, row maps, and
    process-level reproducibility links are retained. The package reports
    numerical curve features but leaves their scientific interpretation to an
    explicitly justified analysis. The method was introduced by Mendoza and
    Araújo (2022) <doi:10.1111/ecog.06289>.
